      "content": "That sounds great for the pitch, but one of the investors is a real stickler for the math. He's going to ask about the p-values. I saw the raw data and noted it was sitting at 0.06. How should I frame the statistical significance in the slides so he doesn't get hung up on the fact that we missed the 0.05 threshold?",
